I'm looking to add a template on an `operator()` overload, something like this:

```
struct Test {
    template<typename T>
    T operator()(const T x) {
        return x;
    }
    
};

[numthreads(32,1,1)]
void main() {
    Test t;
    t(5); // error
    t<uint>(5); // error
    t.operator()<uint>(5); // error
}
```

All syntax tests fail. Here is a link for testing: [Link](https://godbolt.org/z/vx15Ybd1f)
Note that in C++ `test(5)` passes (the compiler infers the type) and `t.operator()<uint>(5)` passes as well.

Thank you in advance
